lede: Legacy, carried lightly and warmly until it isn't (TL).
calls:
k: On the record
Calla Merritt of Saint Meridian, twenty-one. A Broadcast family, and the Broadcast's favorite, because she's what it's decided the Trials should produce without any manipulation required (TR). Her surname is Merritt (Ruling).
||
k: Her fate
note: Her death.
Pushed into the river by Corinne on Endurance Day 2 (TR). Her status goes back to her family, with no compensation and no punishment (FR 24).
/end

@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · V · CALLA · THE RECORD AND HER DOMINION" m="TKC: TR · TL · DOM · RULING; VOL. I · {v1:vane} · {v1:trials-history}"
# Saint Meridian
plate: doc
dh: Covenant Registry | DOMINION OF VANE · SAINT MERIDIAN
df: Candidate | MERRITT, Calla · twenty-one
df: Father | Broadcast, a mid-level editor (TR)
df: Mother | a former Covenant Daughter (TR)
df: Prepared since | childhood (TR)
stamp: COVENANT DAUGHTER
/end
rec:
What she knows | Broadcast cues, camera patterns, the kind of attention that reads as grace on a screen. Her talent is real, and the performance has become her identity (TR).
Her mother | A former Covenant Daughter who withdrew in Phase Three of an earlier Trial (TR). The timeline says the 32nd (TL).
Her Dominion | The legacy Dominion. Some families have sent daughters to three Trials running, and high-scoring girls are prepared for candidacy from the time they can read (DOM). The Broadcast Assessment at sixteen makes exceptional girls minor public figures overnight (DOM).
CONFLICT | The 32nd Trial was in 2097, when Calla was fourteen, and a Covenant Daughter can't already be a mother. INFERENCE: Her mother's Trial was earlier, and the "32nd" belongs to someone or something else.
prompt: Which Trial her mother was in, and why she withdrew | fill

@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · V · CALLA · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 1 OF 2" m="TKC: TR · DOM; VOL. I · {v1:vane} · {v1:lived3}"
# What she believes
rec:
Who taught her | A mother who withdrew and a father who edits (TR). INFERENCE: She learned faith as something performed well.
What she believes | OPEN QUESTION: Whether anything under the performance is hers.
Her Dominion's underground | Ghost Marriages outside registration, and the Ghost Declaration, where a boy says what he actually intends before saying what's required (DOM).
empire: What the Temple teaches about a woman like her
INTERPRETATION: That she's the Trials working as designed. The Broadcast doesn't have to manipulate her, because she already is what it wants (TR).
/end
